        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="jp_cap" parent="jp" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B45309;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#B45309;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Uploading a photo&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#232F3E&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ask the API for an upload link (presigned URL): CloudFront → load balancer → API checks limits&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Response: a presigned URL, valid for minutes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The browser uploads straight to the incoming bucket; S3 answers &quot;uploaded&quot; at once&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;GuardDuty scans the file; EventBridge sends every scan result to the photo processing queue&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The Lambda checks it is a clean scan of this exact version. If not: quarantine/ folder. If clean: Rekognition checks, resize, remove GPS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Approved → photos bucket. Flagged → held/ folder for a moderator. Clean document → documents bucket&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Every result goes to the upload results queue; a worker pulls it from the queue and records it in RDS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#B45309;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;P8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Response: the app asks for the status: approved or under review&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="208" width="1580" x="20" y="1465" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
