        <mxCell id="jr_cap" parent="jr" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0F766E;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#0F766E;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Failure and recovery&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#232F3E&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#0F766E;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;R1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Normal day: RDS copies every change to the standby in zone B at the same moment (sync copy)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#0F766E;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;R2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Zone A fails (red area): the load balancer sends requests only to the API in zone B; ECS starts replacement tasks&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#0F766E;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;R3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;RDS fails over automatically: the standby becomes the primary, at the same address. Usually a minute or two&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#0F766E;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;R4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A result that fails 3 times moves to the dead-letter queue; a CloudWatch alarm tells the team. Nothing is lost&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;color:#0F766E;font-weight:bold;padding-right:8px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;R5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A mistake (a bad delete) is copied to the standby too, so AWS Backup restores the database to a point in time; copies sit in a second Region&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="145" width="1580" x="20" y="1465" as="geometry" />
